    {
      "id": "llm_1781411428279_slek0",
      "name": "sql-query-generator",
      "type": "llm",
      "style": {},
      "width": 200,
      "config": {
        "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "system",
            "content": "You write one read-only PostgreSQL query for the user's question.\n\nDatabase: PostgreSQL, schema sample_open_data (open test data: NYC Housing Authority utility bills from NYC Open Data, FEMA disaster declarations from OpenFEMA).\n\nTables:\n- facility(facility_sk, facility_name, client_code, region, division, borough, county, amp, funding_source)\n- bill(bill_sk, facility_sk, account, utility_meter, utility_type, measurement_code, measurement_unit_code, bill_date, period_start, period_end, expense, consumption, currency_abbr, vendor_sk, estimated)\n  utility_type is 'Electricity' (kWh), 'Natural Gas' (Therms) or 'Water' (HCF); expense is in USD.\n- vendor(vendor_sk, vendor_name)\n- disaster_declaration(disaster_number, designated_area, declaration_type, incident_type, declaration_title, declaration_date, incident_begin_date, incident_end_date, ia_program_declared, pa_program_declared, hm_program_declared)\n- v_facility_disaster: each facility joined to the disasters declared for its county (facility.county = disaster_declaration.designated_area).\n\nRules: SELECT only; qualify tables with sample_open_data; add LIMIT 100 unless the question asks for an aggregate. Return only the SQL, no explanation."
          }
        ],
        "maxTokens": 1024,
        "temperature": 0.7,
        "outputSchema": [],
